WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.240
Brazil’s President Dilma Rousseff is in
political free fall right now.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.260
The lower house, which was dominated really
by her political supporters, voted in spite

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:19.600
of all that to bring charges against her for
cooking the books to hide election year spending.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.170
The senate now has to concur. If it does,
which I think is better than a 50% chance,

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.070
the Senate will then hear those charges formally.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.480
And you have to wonder—how did we get here?

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.879
It goes back actually before her reelection.
The state took such an important role in the

00:00:35.879 --> 00:00:36.329
economy.

00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:41.320
On the other hand, did not modernize the economy
to make it more competitive and help generate

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.520
sustainable economic growth.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:49.030
So consequently, unemployment, an economy
that, really, these policies drove into the

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:49.930
ditch.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:54.219
Undermining the state-run oil company so that
it lost money.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:59.010
And then actually looting the coffers of that
oil company to sustain their own crooked,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.980
crony campaigns.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.289
That's how they got into this mess. And now,
it looks like impeachment is going to run

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:06.170
its course.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.740
The world's attention is about to turn to
Brazil as Rio hosts the Summer Olympics.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.650
Let us know how you think that this economic
and political crisis will affect Brazil's

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:15.810
image in the world.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:20.280
Give us your comments. And also, give us ideas
on what other issues you'd like AEI scholars

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.630
to cover in 60 seconds.

